  "chkFastStartupOn": "Fast Startup is enabled",
  "chkFastStartupHow": "When Fast Startup is enabled, modifying the EFI partition while Windows is shut down may permanently corrupt the EFI partition on the next Windows boot and leave the tablet unbootable. Uncheck “Turn on fast startup” under Control Panel → Power Options → Choose what the power buttons do.",
  "chkFastStartupHowReg": "When Fast Startup is enabled, modifying the EFI partition while Windows is shut down may permanently corrupt the EFI partition on the next Windows boot and leave the tablet unbootable. Run the following command as Administrator to disable Fast Startup: reg add \"HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\Power\" /v HiberbootEnabled /t REG_DWORD /d 0 /f",
  "chkBitlockerOff": "BitLocker is disabled",
  "chkBitlockerOn": "BitLocker is enabled",
  "chkBitlockerUnknown": "Unable to read BitLocker status",
  "chkBitlockerHow": "Before modifying EFI boot files, the installer automatically suspends BitLocker protection (Windows resumes it on its next boot), though boot changes may still cause Windows to prompt for your recovery key. We will require you to enter the correct BitLocker recovery key at a later step to confirm that you will have a working key to unlock Windows if needed. You can retrieve your recovery key at https://aka.ms/myrecoverykey; saving a copy in advance on another device, such as your phone, is recommended.",
  "chkBitlockerHowSecureBoot": "Before disabling Secure Boot, please verify your recovery key and suspend BitLocker protection below.",
  "chkBitlockerConverting": "BitLocker is encrypting or decrypting the system drive",
  "chkBitlockerConvertingHow": "Until the conversion finishes, the installer cannot determine whether Windows will prompt for a recovery key after boot files are modified. Please wait for the operation to finish (check progress in Settings → Privacy & security → Device encryption, or under BitLocker Drive Encryption in Control Panel), then check again. Encryption may pause on battery power, so connecting the power adapter is recommended.",
  "chkBitlockerSuspended": "BitLocker protection is suspended",
  "chkBitlockerSuspendedHow": "The system drive is encrypted, but BitLocker protection is currently suspended or awaiting activation. Windows will not prompt for a recovery key on its next boot.",
  "chkBitlockerNoKey": "No BitLocker recovery key configured for the system drive",
  "chkBitlockerNoKeyHow": "The system drive is encrypted, but no BitLocker recovery key is configured; if Windows enters BitLocker recovery at startup, you will not be able to unlock the system drive. To avoid being locked out of Windows, run “manage-bde -protectors -add C: -RecoveryPassword” as Administrator to generate a recovery key, save it on another device, and check again.",
  "chkBitlockerSuspendBox": "Once verified, the installer will suspend BitLocker protection (Windows automatically resumes protection after two restarts); however, firmware changes or extra restarts may still cause Windows to prompt for your recovery key. We require you to enter the correct BitLocker recovery key here to confirm that you will have a working key to unlock Windows if needed. You can retrieve your recovery key at https://aka.ms/myrecoverykey; saving a copy in advance on another device, such as your phone, is recommended.",
