  "sbPagefile": "Virtual memory paging file",
  "sbPagefileHow": "1. Press Win+R, enter “SystemPropertiesPerformance”, and under Virtual memory on the Advanced tab click Change.\n2. Uncheck “Automatically manage paging file size for all drives”, select C:, choose “No paging file”, click Set, confirm with Yes, and click OK.\n3. Restart the device and shrink the C: volume in Disk Management.\n4. After shrinking, re-enable “Automatically manage paging file size for all drives” and restart the device.",
  "sbHiberfil": "System hibernation file",
  "sbHiberfilHow": "1. Open Terminal as Administrator and run “powercfg /h off” to disable hibernation and remove the hibernation file.\n2. Shrink the C: volume in Disk Management.\n3. If you wish to re-enable hibernation afterwards, run “powercfg /h on” (ensure Fast Startup remains disabled).",
  "sbRestore": "System restore points (shadow copies)",
  "sbRestoreHow": "1. Press Win+R and enter “SystemPropertiesProtection” to open System Protection.\n2. Select C:, click Configure, then click Delete to remove all restore points on this drive.\n3. Shrink the C: volume in Disk Management (deleted restore points cannot be recovered).",
  "sbBitlocker": "BitLocker metadata",
  "sbBitlockerHow": "BitLocker metadata on the system drive cannot be relocated while the drive is encrypted. To free more space, turn off BitLocker (device encryption) in Windows, wait for decryption to finish, shrink the C: volume, and re-enable encryption afterwards. Re-enabling encryption generates a new recovery key — please save it securely.",
  "sbUsn": "NTFS change journal (USN journal)",
  "sbUsnHow": "1. Open Terminal as Administrator and run “fsutil usn deletejournal /d C:” to delete the change journal.\n2. Shrink the C: volume in Disk Management (Windows automatically recreates the journal when needed).",
